# DURABLE REPRO — a `Guard[T]` field reached through a PARAMETER is
# MEMORY-UNSAFE at the `&` face and silently wrong at the assign face, while the
# identical access on a guard LOCAL is correct.
#
# WRONG TODAY — measured IDENTICAL at base `6cf79126` and at the Family-1 tip, so
# PRE-EXISTING and not that round's to fix. All cells `gg check`-CLEAN:
#
#   | cell                                        | result                        |
#   |---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|
#   | `&`-param, `&`-face   `inc(&g.fd)`          | C: SIGSEGV exit 139           |
#   |                                              | LLVM: `llc` HARD-FAILS        |
#   |                                              | `'%v1' … 'i32' but expected 'ptr'` |
#   | `&`-param, assign     `g.fd = 99`           | prints 0, caller unchanged    |
#   | BARE param, MUTATING  `inc(&g.fd)`          | C BUILD FAILS: implicit decl  |
#   |                                              | of `gorget_guard_clone`       |
#   | BARE param, READ-ONLY `print(g.fd)`         | builds, prints 0 (want 10)    |
#   | guard LOCAL (control) `inc(&g.fd)`          | 11 — CORRECT                  |
#
# ⚠ THE MUTATION IS THE DISCRIMINATOR on the bare-param row: a read-only probe
# builds and merely reads 0, while a mutating one fails the C build outright
# (the CoW materialize path for a bare guard param emits a clone helper that does
# not exist). Probing read-only reports a much milder defect and mis-scopes the
# fix — this fixture mutates.
#
# ⚠ NOT the served-at-one-face asymmetry Family-1 closed: BOTH faces are wrong
# here. The face split is what distinguishes this from that class.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): the `&`-param cell behaves exactly as the guard
# LOCAL does — the write reaches the guarded value, printing 11 inside the callee
# and 11 at the caller, because a `&`-parameter is a write-through borrow.
#
# ROOT (verified): `try_resolve_field_place` tests `guard_inner_suffix` against
# `current_type` BEFORE the `pointee_type` deref, so a parameter local typed
# `Ptr(Guard__Inner)` never matches the `Guard__…` name and the guard branch is
# skipped entirely. FIX SHAPE: peel the pointer BEFORE the guard-name test (or
# test both) at the producer — one place closes all four cells.
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE CANNOT RUN UNTIL FIXED: the `&`-param row SIGSEGVs on C and
# produces NO BINARY on LLVM, so there is no output to compare on either lane.
# It is `#[ignore]`d and asserts the intended values; same shape as the in-tree
# `known_gaps/sound_amp_deque_element_field.gg`, which documents its own
# C-SIGSEGV / LLVM-`llc`-fail split.
#
# Cited from TODO.md (widening the generic-indirection guard entry, whose
# "direct guard field access WORKS" premise held only for a guard LOCAL).
# Un-ignore when the producer peels the pointer before the guard-name test.
struct Inner:
    int fd

int seed():
    return 10

void inc(int &n):
    n = n + 1

# THE BROKEN CELL — a guard reached through a `&` parameter.
void via_amp(Guard[Inner] &g):
    inc(&g.fd)
    print(g.fd)

void main():
    Mutex[Inner] m = Mutex[Inner](Inner(seed()))
    Guard[Inner] g = m.lock()
    via_amp(&g)
    print(g.fd)
